Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  giant monsters and Nile ating  skyscrapers colossal lizards roaring  winged Titans as they battle to the  death what could possibly go wrong the  answer so very very much  Godzilla commits so many game design  sins that they become impossible to  count but the greatest horror of them  all is that such giant monsters could be  so boring  it all starts with god of destruction  mode as the king of the monsters you  march out of the sea and begin your  rampage with the epic goal of destroying  the power generators in each level all  the while a g-force operator shouts  military orders for all the good it does  she also announces opportunities for  ground crews to collect data at  particular points that requires you to  click a stick at which point the camera  zooms out to show you a cinematic view  of the creatures flailing  [Music]  you're playing is a giant monster but  simultaneously as the defense forces  it's a bizarre narrative contradiction  that culminates when your military  contact mourns her losses while  triumphant music plays and you're  granted a victory but put aside the dumb  storytelling since it's the least of the  game's problems instead focus on how  leading Godzilla into the fray is like  steering a backhoe through an aquarium  he's heavy  sure but he's in no way fun to maneuver  and so you charge forward swing your  tail and bash buildings to keep yourself  occupied as you trudge towards the  generators over and over again you do it  until you finish the campaign 20 minutes  or so later and realize you have to  repeat it many many times over to unlock  upgrades and other Kazu which you can  also lead into battle the game is built  around unlocks and upgrades which come  at a horrendously slow pace the menus  seem to offer a lot of options but don't  let them fool you Godzilla is very light  on content that it's sold at full retail  price is ludicrous and insulting  other monsters appear to do battle with  you of course the games best moments  aren't related to gameplay but to the  stirring visuals of seeing Rodin or King  Ghidorah appear and clash with  spacegodzilla such events may mirror  Godzilla films but actually taking part  in them reveals a laughable array of  awfulness balance is one of the biggest  problems some monster combinations are  hysterically inept such as when you take  control of King Ghidorah and spam a  diving attack to victory without taking  a lick of damage if you want to be super  cautious force your enemy against some  invisible wall and watch them float into  the air as his animations struggle to  complete ends like several monsters  Batra can surge through the air to  safety then return for a hit-and-run  attack exploiting your opponent's slow  turning speed facing a larva stage  Mothra as an air bound Batra meanwhile  is one of the most tedious and broken  things I've ever done in a video game  that's because only my strongest attack  which is governed by a heat meter was  the only consistent way to do damage  it's boring on top of boring from here  the problems just pile on sometimes the  game Auto targets your enemy even when  you're faced in another direction and  try to charge away you face Super x  aircraft in the campaign but some  attacks have Godzilla clipping right  through them without doing damage and  should you be tempted to fight one or  two players in versus mode crippling lag  and timeouts might have you reaching for  the power button that's a shame because  the most enjoyment I had with Godzilla  was winning a three kaiju free-for-all  with only a smidgen of health remaining  keep in mind however that I didn't earn  that victory  I just knew which attacks to spam and so  it goes in this overpriced and  unattractive game whose finest mode is  one in which you place unlockable action  figures on a diorama yes looking at  static monster figures in fighting poses  is a lot more fun than actually  participating in battle the worst news  of all is that if you want more figures  you have to play the game and  that's just not worth all the yawns  [Music]  you  [Music]

